{"agent_id":"pp3g-n9vG-review-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-f670","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:31:12.695454868Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"563a7d84-b3d1-4525-8cfb-7906cf81e9c4","comment_uuid":"a0a8cf77-e170-4af8-84f9-dd756f8971a5","author":"pp3g-n9vG-review-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-f670","content":"Plan: INDEPENDENT review of the #175 design against live evidence, not just prose. Method: (1) re-verify the design's factual claims directly in the installed 1.18.12 binary (embedded plaintext JS) — guard presence/count, SessionRetry.policy schedule shape, MessageV2.fromError mapping, halt() logError path, per-request AbortController; (2) audit the proposed wrapBody/dispatcher patch for stream-semantics correctness (backpressure, timer lifecycle, controller state, header copying); (3) stress-test the Option A vs Option B framing for a missing third option; (4) assess retry-cap blast radius against the rate-limit/retry-after code paths; (5) check rebuild/replace/rollback commands for atomicity + prerequisites (bun, network, disk) and upgrade-survival against the actual launch chain (claude wrapper -> ~/.local/bin/opencode -> REAL); (6) grade the verification matrix for coverage gaps. Verdict PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL with required fixes.","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:31:12.688858055Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:HSE7SGijpZijCJVSfcgbiifYOl9LfT6cnGsBQz/2eIA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgINhBbmb8rdoOOUU0A6fKQ2bIlMPSORkyrJnuMJfZNugAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAUTnfnjVNuPu513MOugkuFpiprJSXRkmYiQIegjMx8Yxcl55E7V431ZbVMkNTcq20IxHTkKMcc4Pxe60ZSe4YCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:HSE7SGijpZijCJVSfcgbiifYOl9LfT6cnGsBQz/2eIA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgINhBbmb8rdoOOUU0A6fKQ2bIlMPSORkyrJnuMJfZNugAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPx9rkYQ0O74BqltGy98yU7V2MclCzo5FG6w3aaxEV4LI7AWvGDoTcZMCVqvhQ